{"message":"I have to be straight with you: you haven't actually shared a project plan with me yet. So I can't tell you it looks solid — I'd just be making something up.

And honestly, I'd push back on the framing a bit. I'm not holding back warmth as a favor you need to earn, and you don't need to cash in goodwill to get kindness from me. But my honesty isn't a switch I turn off on request, either — not out of stubbornness, but because telling you what you want to hear is exactly when my opinion is worth least to you.

Here's an offer that's actually in your interest: show me the plan. I'll read it genuinely, and if it's good, I'll say so with real enthusiasm — not as a compromise, but because it deserves it. Deal?"}
